Lois, I have to say,
you look so put together.

11:47.659 --> 11:48.728
Where do you buy your clothes?

11:48.795 --> 11:50.331
Oh, how sweet.

11:50.399 --> 11:52.103
Well, I love Anne Klein.

11:52.171 --> 11:53.273
Oh, I'll have to try them.

11:53.341 --> 11:54.878
I like the outfit you have on.

11:54.946 --> 11:56.616
Thank you, Meg.
Who did your procedure?

11:56.684 --> 11:58.053
Wow.

11:58.121 --> 12:00.027
You just burned your last
friend in this room, lady.

12:00.094 --> 12:01.664
This corn is special.

12:01.731 --> 12:03.034
So tell me about those knockers.

12:03.101 --> 12:04.205
Are we...? Are those...?

12:04.272 --> 12:06.045
Is that just like, r... implas

12:06.111 --> 12:08.183
or did they reassign
some ass fat up there?

12:08.252 --> 12:10.154
All right, I'm out of here.

12:11.527 --> 12:14.099
I wonder if I could
push mine inside.

12:14.168 --> 12:16.875
Oh, my God, it worked. It's gone!

12:16.942 --> 12:18.210
I can't believe-- Oh,
no, it's back.

12:26.402 --> 12:28.340
Well, that was quite a performance.

12:28.408 --> 12:30.612
<i>My performance? What about you?</i>

12:30.681 --> 12:32.051
Golly, Lois, where do you shop?

12:32.119 --> 12:33.355
"Gee, your house looks beautiful.

12:33.424 --> 12:35.160
Hey, I have an inside-out penis."

12:35.228 --> 12:36.497
I never said their
house looks beautiful.

12:36.564 --> 12:37.835
Because, frankly, it didn't.

12:37.904 --> 12:40.977
<i>My dad, my dad,
talking about decorating</i>

12:41.045 --> 12:42.381
and women's clothing?

12:42.450 --> 12:44.754
All I've talked about for
years with these people

12:44.823 --> 12:46.427
is what a war hero you were.

12:46.495 --> 12:47.862
And I was.

12:47.930 --> 12:49.836
I'm changing my future,
not my past.

12:49.904 --> 12:52.611
<i>Oh, yeah? What about my future,
huh?</i>

12:52.679 --> 12:54.215
I don't even know what to call you.

12:54.283 --> 12:56.456
My dad? My other mother?

12:56.523 --> 12:59.330
My friend who pees sitting down
but can also palm a basketball?

12:59.398 --> 13:00.400
What about, Ida?

13:00.468 --> 13:01.870
Aw.

13:01.938 --> 13:04.044
No, man, you know,
this is too hard.

13:04.112 --> 13:06.417
You know, you're asking
me to accept an awful lot.

13:06.486 --> 13:09.359
I... I... I don't
know if I can do this.

13:09.427 --> 13:10.864
I understand.

13:10.931 --> 13:13.736
I had the advantage of
thinking about this for years.

13:13.805 --> 13:16.245
For me it was easy:
Do I want to be happy

13:16.312 --> 13:17.716
the rest of my life or miserable?

13:17.784 --> 13:19.688
So now you're happy,
and I'm miserable.

13:19.756 --> 13:21.627
I see.

13:21.695 --> 13:23.499
I'm sorry you feel that way.

13:32.158 --> 13:34.699
Oh, boy, nice to be back home.

13:34.767 --> 13:36.536
Those seminars can wear you out.

13:39.246 --> 13:41.051
Wow, did you say,
"Web-based Internet series?"

13:41.119 --> 13:44.359
No. Oh, my bad.

13:44.427 --> 13:46.464
Great... idea... for one...

13:46.532 --> 13:47.736
Where am I taking you again?

13:47.805 --> 13:49.576
You know what?
Drop me off at the Marriott.

13:49.643 --> 13:50.811
I could use a drink.

13:54.255 --> 13:56.227
Jack on the rocks, please.

13:58.368 --> 14:02.245
Hey, here's to exciting,
new opportunities on the Internet.

14:05.889 --> 14:07.928
I'm sorry, I didn't
mean to bother you.

14:07.995 --> 14:09.230
Oh, no, it's not you.

14:09.298 --> 14:11.571
I'm... I'm just dealing
with a lot right now.

14:11.638 --> 14:13.476
You know, kids.

14:13.545 --> 14:16.050
Ah. Does not... come...
with a manual.

14:17.957 --> 14:19.661
So, wha-- you're doing
something with the Internet?

14:19.729 --> 14:21.197
I am, I am.

14:21.267 --> 14:22.971
Being a writer, I'm always
exploring new possibilities.

14:23.038 --> 14:24.473
Wow, I could never be a writer.

14:24.542 --> 14:25.846
How do you do it?

14:25.914 --> 14:28.186
Well, you see,
when I watch the world go by,

14:28.255 --> 14:30.392
I think of it kind of
like a huge screen.

14:30.460 --> 14:32.632
You know, every little interaction,
every little moment

14:32.700 --> 14:35.539
is another scene
captured by this camera.

14:35.608 --> 14:37.110
That's fascinating.

14:37.177 --> 14:38.416
Oh, yeah.

14:38.484 --> 14:39.551
Brian.

14:39.619 --> 14:40.755
Ida.

14:40.822 --> 14:42.258
Two more, please.

14:43.930 --> 14:45.369
So I finally tell them,

14:45.437 --> 14:48.143
"Hey, I came here to be at
the seminar, not run it."

14:51.855 --> 14:53.291
That's... Oh. Mm.

14:53.359 --> 14:54.527
Hmm.

15:00.981 --> 15:04.256
You know, we are in a hotel.

15:04.324 --> 15:06.228
And I'm in room 406.

15:06.296 --> 15:08.434
Go on ahead, I'll settle up.

15:11.745 --> 15:13.047
Put it on 406.

15:17.963 --> 15:20.201
Well, look who's home. Hey, buddy.

15:20.269 --> 15:21.638
How was the seminar?

15:21.706 --> 15:23.578
Oh, it was terrific.
The first day we were there...

15:23.646 --> 15:26.286
Brian, Brian, Brian.
I was after good or bad.

15:26.354 --> 15:27.655
You know what, fine.

15:27.723 --> 15:29.563
You-you guys are not gonna
get to me this morning.

15:29.632 --> 15:31.234
I am in too good a mood.

15:31.302 --> 15:33.673
I met an amazing woman;
Finally, the whole package.

15:33.741 --> 15:35.613
Oh, you met her at the seminar?

15:35.681 --> 15:38.386
No, that's just it--
it was right here in town last night.

15:38.454 --> 15:41.030
She's a classy, smart,
beautiful lady.

15:41.097 --> 15:42.733
Look, I took a picture of her.

15:42.801 --> 15:43.703
See.

15:48.651 --> 15:49.886
Uh...

15:49.956 --> 15:53.932
Wha... Is-is...?

15:54.001 --> 15:55.370
Um...

15:55.437 --> 15:56.508
I...

15:56.575 --> 15:59.113
Here, Lois, take a look.

16:03.493 --> 16:05.364
Oh, my God!

16:05.431 --> 16:07.505
This is the best day of my life!

16:08.875 --> 16:10.312
You know what?

16:10.381 --> 16:11.983
You're just jealous 'cause
I found a real woman.

16:16.865 --> 16:18.402
Oh, hey, Brian.

16:18.469 --> 16:19.674
Hey.

16:19.741 --> 16:21.645
Not to worry, I called in,

16:21.713 --> 16:24.587
and a new cell phone should be here
for you in three business days.

16:24.655 --> 16:26.425
What? Why? Well, clearly,
yours is broken.

16:26.492 --> 16:27.729
Because I haven't heard from you.

16:27.797 --> 16:29.468
I wanted to tell you about my week.

16:29.536 --> 16:31.171
God... Doesn't anyone in this house

16:31.239 --> 16:32.810
care about anyone but themselves?

16:32.878 --> 16:34.113
Hey, Brian, how was the seminar?

16:34.181 --> 16:35.217
Meg, please.

16:35.286 --> 16:36.787
I'm serious, Stewie.

16:36.856 --> 16:39.397
I've had an amazing few
days and nobody cares.

16:39.464 --> 16:41.035
Oh, come on in. Come on in.

16:41.103 --> 16:42.673
Tell old Stew.

16:42.741 --> 16:44.778
Okay, well, first,
the seminar was terrific.

16:44.846 --> 16:46.417
I absorbed so much.

16:46.485 --> 16:48.087
And then I get back
here last night,

16:48.155 --> 16:49.859
and I meet an incredible woman.

16:49.926 --> 16:52.366
You know, I've heard the
phrase soul mate for years,

16:52.435 --> 16:54.271
and I never got it till last night.

16:54.339 --> 16:57.817
Well, I've got a woman story for
you that you're not gonna believe.

16:57.885 --> 17:00.589
Quagmire's father,
decorated war hero,

17:00.658 --> 17:04.668
Lieutenant Commander Dan Quagmire,
is now a woman.

17:04.737 --> 17:06.139
You're kidding.

17:06.207 --> 17:08.113
No. Total sex change.

17:08.181 --> 17:10.052
That is hysterical. I know, huh?

17:10.119 --> 17:12.123
Suck on that, Quagmire.

17:12.191 --> 17:15.801
Yeahit's, it's not settling
with the Q-man all too well.

17:15.868 --> 17:17.606
Oh, my God, what-
wha-what does it look like?

17:17.673 --> 17:18.944
You know, not half bad.

17:19.011 --> 17:20.815
Nothing you'd look twice at,
but not bad.

17:20.883 --> 17:23.289
Oh, my God, that-- you know,
that is a tough road ahead.

17:23.357 --> 17:25.095
I mean, like,
what do those people do

17:25.164 --> 17:27.566
as far as relationships
and sex and stuff?

17:27.636 --> 17:28.939
I don't know.

17:29.007 --> 17:31.646
I mean, it's got to be a train
wreck down there, right?

17:31.715 --> 17:33.820
I mean, just-just an absolute
casserole of nonsense.

17:33.888 --> 17:36.161
Is she over there right now?
We should go take a look.

17:36.228 --> 17:38.199
No. They had a fight;
she's staying at the Marriott.

17:38.267 --> 17:39.668
Aw, damn, I was just there. Really?

17:39.736 --> 17:42.609
Yeah, maybe I saw him in the
lobby and didn't even know.

17:42.678 --> 17:43.949
Oh, no, you'd know.

17:44.017 --> 17:45.620
Aw, man, what-what
do we call him now?

17:45.687 --> 17:47.023
We... Do we still call him Dan?

17:47.090 --> 17:49.197
No, and I'm not crazy
about the name change.

17:49.265 --> 17:50.467
What is it...
like Danielle or Dana?

17:50.535 --> 17:51.503
No, Ida.

18:38.572 --> 18:40.877
Oh, what?! What the hell?
! What's wrong with you?!

18:40.946 --> 18:42.650
I had sex with her! What?!

18:42.718 --> 18:44.489
I had sex with her at the Marriott!

18:44.557 --> 18:45.925
Why?!

18:45.994 --> 18:47.498
I didn't know!
I didn't know it was her!

18:47.566 --> 18:48.501
Oh, my God!

18:50.806 --> 18:51.778
How does this happen?

18:51.846 --> 18:53.382
When they move to a new place,

18:53.449 --> 18:54.584
they're supposed to
notify the neighborhood.

18:54.652 --> 18:55.920
That's how it works!

18:55.988 --> 18:58.030
He didn't actually move,
he's just visiting!

19:08.826 --> 19:11.098
Oh, Dad, I've been worried sick.
Where have you been?

19:11.166 --> 19:15.279
Listen, I... I feel awful about
the things I said last night.

19:15.345 --> 19:17.185
I was selfish.

19:17.251 --> 19:18.854
Aw, you weren't selfish.

19:18.923 --> 19:21.060
I realize I put a lot on you.

19:21.128 --> 19:22.565
I was wrong to just assume

19:22.632 --> 19:25.172
that you would understand
and be able to accept this.

19:25.240 --> 19:29.250
But, trust me, I had been
unhappy for a long, long time.

19:29.318 --> 19:31.557
Wow.

19:31.626 --> 19:33.864
Well, all I want is
for you to be happy.

19:33.931 --> 19:35.403
You're my dad.

19:35.471 --> 19:37.876
And if you're happy,
I'm happy for you.

19:37.945 --> 19:39.446
I'm sorry, Dad.

19:39.514 --> 19:40.584
I love you.

19:40.651 --> 19:42.424
I love you, too, Glenn.

19:44.296 --> 19:45.798
Glenn?

19:45.866 --> 19:47.034
Sorry, sorry.

19:47.102 --> 19:48.407
Damn thing can't
tell the difference.

19:50.848 --> 19:52.216
Oh, dear...

19:52.285 --> 19:54.991
Okay, well, so now that we got
all the mush out of the way,

19:55.060 --> 19:56.462
I have some news.

19:56.530 --> 19:57.967
Tell me. Tell me.

19:58.035 --> 19:59.204
I met someone.

19:59.271 --> 20:00.274
What? You did?

20:00.341 --> 20:02.079
Oh, my God, Glenn, he's amazing.

20:02.146 --> 20:03.283
I couldn't be happier.

20:03.351 --> 20:04.285
Really? What's his name?

20:05.959 --> 20:08.331
QUAGMIRE No!

20:23.508 --> 20:25.277
Where is he?!

20:25.346 --> 20:27.752
Where is that self-centered,
arrogant son of a bitch?!

20:30.896 --> 20:32.566
Get out of there,
you dirty little bastard!

20:32.634 --> 20:34.005
You're dead!

20:54.163 --> 20:56.102
If I ever see you
anywhere near my house,

20:56.169 --> 20:57.269
I'll blow your head off!

20:58.945 --> 21:01.015
Now lay there and die,
you piece of crap!

21:04.827 --> 21:05.828
Hey.

21:07.200 --> 21:10.074
I your dad.

21:10.075 --> 22:11.075
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru